\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2.1}{\ignorespaces The residual TemporalBlock used in every TCN of this thesis: two weight-normalised dilated causal 1-D convolutions, each followed by a ReLU and dropout, summed with a residual connection (kernel size~3).}}{10}{figure.caption.8}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2.2}{\ignorespaces A single LSTM cell at time step $t$: the forget, input, and output gates regulate how the cell state $C_t$ and hidden state $h_t$ are updated from the previous states $C_{t-1}$, $h_{t-1}$ and the input $x_t$.}}{11}{figure.caption.9}%
\addvspace {10\p@ }
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3.1}{\ignorespaces Engagement class distribution by dataset.}}{16}{figure.caption.11}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3.2}{\ignorespaces Class distribution by split, per dataset.}}{17}{figure.caption.12}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3.3}{\ignorespaces Semantic-group hybrid architecture. Each OpenFace group is encoded independently into a 64-d embedding (group encoders are chosen per group from TCN / Transformer (T) / LSTM); the I3D clip vector is encoded by an MLP into a 128-d embedding. The six embeddings are concatenated (448-d) and classified by a shared MLP; each stream also feeds an auxiliary head. The OpenFace-only variant drops the I3D row and fuses a 320-d vector.}}{19}{figure.caption.14}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3.4}{\ignorespaces The three interchangeable per-group encoders. Each maps a group's $T\times D_{\text {group}}$ sequence to a 64-dimensional embedding through temporal mean-pooling and layer normalisation; one is chosen independently for each of the five groups.}}{20}{figure.caption.15}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3.5}{\ignorespaces Baseline \texttt {openface\_mlp}: the full $T\times 709$ OpenFace sequence is flattened and classified by a multilayer perceptron.}}{21}{figure.caption.16}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3.6}{\ignorespaces Baseline \texttt {openface\_tcn}: a temporal convolutional network over the full 709-d sequence, adaptively average-pooled and classified.}}{21}{figure.caption.17}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3.7}{\ignorespaces Baseline \texttt {openface\_lstm}: a two-layer LSTM over the full 709-d sequence whose final state is classified.}}{21}{figure.caption.18}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3.8}{\ignorespaces Baseline \texttt {openface\_transformer}: a Transformer encoder over the full 709-d sequence with sinusoidal positional encoding, mean-pooled and classified.}}{22}{figure.caption.19}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3.9}{\ignorespaces Baseline \texttt {i3d\_mlp}: the pooled 1024-d I3D clip vector is classified by a multilayer perceptron.}}{22}{figure.caption.20}%
